    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/forensic/watermark/video/v1` \"Forensic Watermark (Video)\"** (gate 34 — the FORENSIC pack opens; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Capability tier (fs.write/temp for the mask PNG, one engine ffmpeg pass per probe). Props = pure defaults on `hero_4.mp4` (1280×720 · 25 fps · 12.16 s, person typing — flat wall + keyboard, the surfaces where a mark shows). The output IS that clip, marked with payload `deadbeef`; the `.watermark.json` sidecar lands beside it.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | capability · not internal · not deprecated | confirm — base (provenance is a category baseline; the verify half ships with it) |\n| Label | \"Forensic Watermark (Video)\" | keep |\n| Cover / Tutorial | none / none | skip — `renderLite` (NEW) shows the picked clip above a \"NOT YET EMBEDDED\" band, so selection never probes the source |\n| Previews | `preview.png` 1920×1080 (07-14, your brand-M \"FORENSIC WATERMARK\" illustration) | LEAVE AS-IS (committed founder asset; a marked frame is indistinguishable from the source, so an illustration is the honest face) — say if you want an mp4 |\n| Battery | 13 embed cases + 7 re-encode channels + 13 verify canvases GREEN after fixes (below) | — |\n| E2E | 1 variant (id32 on hero_1) + env-gated round-trip suite | — |\n| Acceptance | **your social round-trip** (IG / X / YouTube / TikTok) — kit in `SOCIAL-ROUNDTRIP.md` beside this file | run after the default verdict |\n\n**Your two notes, addressed:**\n\n*\"the watermark is actually sorta visible on renders\"* — confirmed: a hard per-cell ±1.5-luma step on smooth gradients reads as a faint checkerboard (2× crop of the wall in the old default vs the new one is in the stress set as **stress-10 = the old default** for A/B). Tuned with two new mechanisms, measured on three clips (flat-region RMS of out−src where the SOURCE is smooth; decode margin native + after a 1 Mbps re-encode):\n\n| Variant (hero_4 bright / hero_2 dark night / hero_5 textured) | flat RMS | worst \\|score\\| native → 1 Mbps |\n|---|---|---|\n| OLD default: uniform α 0.012, hard cells | 1.88 / 1.53 / 1.79 | 16.2→14.2 / 8.0→1.1 / 12.7→11.4 |\n| uniform 0.012 + soft edges 0.15 | 1.81 / 1.43 / 1.67 | 12.6→12.0 / 3.8→1.4 / 9.8→9.3 |\n| uniform 0.008 + soft 0.15 | 1.56 / 0.83 / 1.43 | 8.2→8.4 / 3.6→0.4 / 4.3→3.8 |\n| **NEW default: adaptive [0.004..0.02] × texture mask + soft 0.15** | **1.10 / 0.37 / 1.05** | 7.0→6.8 / 3.1→0.2 / 6.2→5.8 |\n| adaptive [0.003..0.018] + soft 0.25 | 1.06 / 0.35 / 1.03 | 5.9→5.6 / 1.3→0.2 / 5.2→4.7 |\n\nMechanisms: (1) **texture mask** — the source is probed a second time at 2× the grid; a cell's activity (spread of its 2×2 sub-cells) scales α from `alphaMin` on flat cells (walls, sky, gradients) up to the luminance bell on textured ones — the mark moves to where the eye can't see it; (2) **soft cell edges** (`edgeSoftness`, mask blurred by 0.15 of a cell) — the step becomes a low-frequency bump, the cell interior the decoder integrates keeps its offset. All 1 Mbps squeezes still PASS (BCH corrects the weak bits); the dark-clip 1 Mbps worst-bit is the number to watch on TikTok. The `alphaMin`/`alphaMax` knobs that were declared but never wired are now the adaptive curve's floor/ceiling.\n\n*\"real testing on social media as part of acceptance\"* — `SOCIAL-ROUNDTRIP.md`: one master per aspect (never let a platform re-frame), upload, download, verify each copy; `contentRect` (new verify knob) for copies a platform letterboxed, with the `cropdetect` one-liner to find the rect. Measured locally: PASS at 500 kbps, double re-encode, and a uniform downscale (the grid is aspect-relative — only crops/pads break it; the \"does not survive scale change\" header was over-cautious).\n\n**Pre-audit findings → fixed:**\n\n| Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Output was the 1920×1080 / 10 s / 30 fps HINT: a 720p 12 s 25 fps clip came back upscaled, cut to 10 s, resampled | Source-follow: 1-step `emit:\"multi\"` pipeline (blur-regions pattern) whose step declares the source's size/fps/duration — verified 720p, 960×540 29.97→30, portrait, 4K 24 fps 10 s, AAC audio intact. An explicit `--durationMs`/Make Duration still wins (3 s pin verified). Make's canvas is IGNORED (as for every source-follow media template) — D1 below |\n| Spawned bare `ffmpeg` from PATH → packaged desktop / toolchain-less host = ERROR card | Probe goes through the engine: `ctx.analysis.cellLuminance` (new; core `probeCellLuminance`, toolchain-bound — your \"templates PULL analysis\" ruling). CLI `.mosaicx`/`resolve` + desktop `.mosaicx` routes now pass `ffmpegPath` like `make` did. Same filtergraph for embed + verify, locked in core |\n| **Portrait sources FAILED to decode (\\|score\\| 0.02)** — sharp's default `fit:\"cover\"` center-cropped the 16:9 cell grid onto the 9:16 canvas, keeping ~20 of 64 columns | `fit:\"fill\"` (the grid stretches onto the canvas); lock in maskAsset.test; portrait now \\|score\\| 13.4 |\n| Selecting the template in Make ran the real `render()` in design mode (ffmpeg probe over the whole source + mask PNG on every keystroke) | `renderLite` stand-in (clip + band); `hasRenderLite` also makes Make hand the real renderable to the render hero |\n| CLI `.mosaicx` route rendered the \"no inputs\" USAGE CARD for every recipe of this template (`hasMediaInputsAlready` knew only `sourceId`/`sourceIds`; ours is `videoPath`) — this ledger could not render at all | any filled `media`-typed schema prop counts as input (`mosaicxRunner.ts`, +test) |\n| `alphaMin`/`alphaMax` declared, never wired (\"reserved for v2\") | wired (adaptive curve); `hostLuminanceGrid` test hatch hidden from the form (`ui.hidden`, agent consumer); every knob has a `ui.label` |\n\n**Design questions for you (D):**\n- **D1 source-follow vs canvas:** output = input envelope, Make canvas ignored (blur-regions precedent). Alternative: honour an explicit canvas and cover-crop. I recommend follow — a forensic copy that re-frames the picture isn't the delivered asset.\n- **D2 uuid128 grid:** the 255-bit code on the default 64×36 grid has 9 cells/bit → margin ~1 (marginal). stress-03 uses 96×54 (20 cells/bit, 130 KB sidecar). Options: mode-aware default grid (the form would then show a value the render didn't use — your \"props must reflect the render\" ruling argues against), or leave + document (current). Or a `cellsPerBit` diagnostic on the card.\n- **D3 `contentRect` manual vs auto:** manual now; an ffmpeg `cropdetect` auto mode in the engine is the follow-up if the social round-trip needs it often.\n- **D4 preview mp4** for the video template, or keep the illustration?\n\n**Not touched:** the BCH/mask math (`@m0saic/template-utils` forensic), sidecar `watermark/v1` shape (only `embed.luminanceAdaptive` now truthfully reports the default), the committed e2e fixture pair (still decodes; README notes re-minting now follows the source).\n\nStress ×10 pre-minted in `stress/` (AAC · dark · uuid128 96×54 · 3 s pin · portrait · 4K · coarse 32×18 · deliberately visible 0.03 hard · fine 128×72 · the OLD default for A/B) — agent pass: every render decodes PASS; review after the default verdict. Renders + verify cards in `stress/renders/`.\n",
    "question": "Gate-34 verdict on the DEFAULT face (hero_4 marked; play it, look for the checkerboard on the wall/keyboard — then A/B the `edgeSoftness 0` + `luminanceAdaptive off` stress-10 twin) · keep the tuned defaults (adaptive on, soft edges 0.15)? · source-follow (output = input envelope, Make canvas ignored) OK? · then the social round-trip (SOCIAL-ROUNDTRIP.md) and stress-01..10."
